22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
 My question is for Mr. D'Souza.

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
 On February 10th, the city launched its Cycling Network Review

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:28,000
 with the mayor saying Montrealers felt they had not been listened to.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
 Results are due by years and after a consultation this fall.

26
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,000
 On October 6th, the borough announced that one direction on the Terbon bike lane

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
 will become winter parking with change before Christmas.

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
 Its stated purpose is parking, not safety,

29
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
 and city documents suggest that the weakest data was used

30
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
 and the city engineers have resisted.

31
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:09,000
 NDG residents who vote overwhelmingly for Peter McQueen

32
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
 were promised they will be heard.

33
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
 Our councillor has been excluded from this entire process.

34
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
 Changing the lane now means ignoring our choice

35
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
 and risk contracting the city's own finding.

36
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
 Will the city ask the borough to wait for the review it promises

37
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
 before changing the Terbon lane?

38
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
 Alexandre, Monsieur Tedeosco.

39
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
 Madame la Présidente, I'll take the question.

40
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
 Thank you, James, for your question.

41
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
 It's sad that we didn't see you yesterday at Café Citoyens

42
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
